# The fixture commits off the main line, each with the fixture commit it was
# made on: a pull request's head, a branch's commit, a squash merge. Each
# folder named here is the whole repository at that commit, as for `history`;
# the fake (e2e/guest/fake-github.py) hashes them into real git ids with that
# parent, and serves them by id — a branch, a pull request or `main` in
# `state.json` points at one by its name. A third name is the folder a commit
# takes its content from, when that is another commit's: a new commit, on its
# own parent, with the same tree.
#
# pr3: pull request #3's head, made on c1 — uptime 1.0.1, asking for what 1.0.0
# asks, and asks-nothing, a new plugin asking for no permission at all.
pr3 c1
# s1: pull request #3 squash-merged onto c1 as exactly its head — pr3's content,
# so every plugin folder in it has pr3's tree (plugins.a-merged-pull-request-becomes-verified).
s1 c1 pr3
# s2: pull request #3 squash-merged onto c1 with a maintainer's change — uptime
# 1.0.2, asking for what 1.0.1 asks; asks-nothing as in pr3
# (plugins.merged-with-changes-offers-the-verified).
s2 c1
# m1: the default branch moved on past s1 — uptime changed again, to s2's 1.0.2
# (plugins.merged-then-moved-on-becomes-verified).
m1 s1 s2
# p2: pull request #3's next commit, made on its head pr3 — uptime's script with
# one paragraph more, the same version and the same manifest, so that nothing a
# read of it fetches is new (plugins.unverified-only-offers,
# plugins.a-branch-is-followed).
p2 pr3
# p2x: pull request #3's head pushed again with its history rewritten — p2's
# content made on c1, not on pr3, so that it does not continue what was
# installed from pr3 (plugins.force-push-is-said).
p2x c1 p2
